   "author": "achow101",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:1779998510"
   ],
   "blocking": true,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "5f7fdc05f62c5ae40a995aaf8e2d4289658cec67"
   },
   "harm": "Rejecting Bech32 strings with multiple '1's breaks valid addresses because '1' is allowed in the HRP.",
   "hash": "5df680e7e5f1dcc9",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:24:04+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:1566472098",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:1566472098",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "This is incorrect. 1 is an allowed character in the human readable part, hence a multiple separators check doesn't make sense.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2024-09-29",
    "by": "portlandhodl",
    "id": "rc:1779998510",
    "quote": "Thank you for this insight, the faulty logic has been removed as a part of the rebase/refactor in the most recent commit."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/27260#discussion_r1566472098"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2024-04-16",
   "author": "achow101",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:1567835969",
    "rc:1779998302"
   ],
   "blocking": true,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "5f7fdc05f62c5ae40a995aaf8e2d4289658cec67"
   },
   "harm": "Dynamically calculating Base58 prefixes from version bytes creates unnecessary maintenance burden when static chainparams suffice.",
   "hash": "2e4a25391f368705",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:24:04+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:1567767610",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:1567767610",
   "kind": "maintenance",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "It seems a bit odd to me to do all of this work to compute these prefixes just for error messaging. ISTM it would be a lot simpler to just hard code them into chainparams anyways... Merging this code seems like an additional maintenance burden for very little gain.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2024-09-29",
    "by": "portlandhodl",
    "id": "rc:1779998302",
    "quote": "The choice to use chainparams to store the Base58 address prefixes has been utilized in the most recent pull. This solution simplifies the PR a noticeable amount."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/27260#discussion_r1567767610"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-04-20",
   "author": "l0rinc",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:4283207812"
   ],
   "blocking": true,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "Bundling large refactors, moves, deletions, and behavior changes across commits impedes review and risks regressions.",
   "hash": "3ee8def64a0d2528",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:24:04+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "r:4137958021",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "r:4137958021",
   "kind": "maintenance",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "my biggest concern (unrelated changes intertwined in big commits and commit messages not explaining the change) is still unaddressed. I have a hard time reviewing this meaningfully - without redoing everything locally, which I would like to avoid.",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/27260#pullrequestreview-4137958021"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-04-20",
   "author": "l0rinc",
   "author_replies": [],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "Using std::string_view instead of std::string in chainparams risks lifetime bugs.",
   "hash": "c53fc4230ac091ea",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:24:04+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3109233352",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3109233352",
   "kind": "safety",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "SSO should already make these cheap, let's use std::string instead. That's consistent with the rest of CChainParams and removes the potential lifetime footgun.",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/27260#discussion_r3109233352"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-04-20",
   "author": "l0rinc",
   "author_replies": [],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "Reparsing the input string during validation causes redundant decoding passes.",
   "hash": "e939a715eca4a5f5",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:24:04+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3109384777",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3109384777",
   "kind": "approach",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "Do we really need to reparse str here? Could we instead have a single path that lowers up front to avoid duplicated work?",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/27260#discussion_r3109384777"
  }
